he factory normalizes the meta‑schema URI to the internal canonical form', 'description': 'Verifies that when a schema declares its own $id and $schema (draft‑06), the factory records them correctly and applies any internal normalization logic.'}]}, {'group': 'Unsupported keyword – should still create schema', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new URI("http://example.com/unknown-key.json")'}, {'parameter': 'schemaNode', 'value': 'new ObjectMapper().readTree("{\\"type\\":\\"object\\",\\"unknownKeyword\\":123}")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'returns a non‑null JsonSchema; validation of the schema itself is not performed here, so the unknown keyword does not cause an exception', 'description': 'Ensures that the factory does not validate the content of the schema during creation; unknown keywords are tolerated at this stage.'}]}, {'group': 'Array schema with items subschema', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new URI("http://example.com/array-schema.json")'}, {'parameter': 'schemaNode', 'value': 'new ObjectMapper().readTree("{\\"type\\":\\"array\\",\\"items\\":{\\"type\\":\\"string\\"}}")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'returns a non‑null JsonSchema where getSchemaNode().path("items").path("type").asText() equals \'string\'', 'description': 'Tests that an array schema with an embedded items subschema triggers the appropriate branch in doCreate and the items node is correctly attached.'}]}, {'group': 'Schema node missing explicit type – still creates', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new URI("http://example.com/no-type.json")'}, {'parameter': 'schemaNode', 'value': 'new ObjectMapper().readTree("{\\"properties\\":{\\"age\\":{\\"type\\":\\"integer\\"}}}")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': "returns a non‑null JsonSchema; the node is accepted even though the top‑level 'type' keyword is absent", 'description': "Ensures that the factory does not require a top‑level 'type' keyword; schemas that rely on implicit object type should still be instantiated."}]}]
